Z||000000||ounmongk||05-19-2000||05:40 PM||||just want to double check a few things... I did a search on the forum and found that there's a weird way of replacing the coolant. ..<P>Here's what I'm going to do, please correct me where I'm wrong.. <P>1. drain the old coolant(of course)<BR>2. pull the radiator cap, fill till it reaches top<BR>3. pull the 'stat, fill till that reaches top<BR>4. let idle for about 10 minutes ( is that right?) <BR>5. see if coolant level in either 'stat or radiator location has gone down..if so, add more coolant.<BR>6. once it's topped off, replace both ('stat and radiator cap...)<BR>7. top off the resovior &lt;sp?&gt; <BR>8 let the car go through it's heat cycle.. <P>I KNOW I've let out some steps... my dad has my Hayes manual for some reason. ( HE DOESN"T EVEN OWN A FIERO!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><BR>anything I should consider? I want to do this before the weather (and sun) gets too hot. TIA<BR>||||reg||1
